Z||000000||phillip||03-16-2000||07:15 PM||||<BR>i have an indy air scoop on my fiero. though it said not intended to be functional i worked it so i could make it so later(i'm not really interested in working out routing for my 2.5, but if i can change engines i want to).has anyone done this ? any ideas appreciated.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||03-17-2000||02:25 AM||||My Indy scoop is functional. I also have changed the mounting so I have a 3" X 6" hole. I drilled 4 large holes in the intake of the scoop and covered it with an 1/8" stainless steel screen. I intend to duct it to the intake of my V-6 This spring. I have to find an air cleaner to replace the original Fiero one. Right now it just keeps the engine compartment nice and cool.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/scoop1.jpg"> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||1FST2M6||03-17-2000||07:58 AM||||OK sorry this is totaly off the subject.. where did you guys get them? ||||reg||1
