Z||000010||Oreif||03-18-2000||12:41 AM||||I don't have any close-up's of the mount I use yet. I'm going to try and get some by next weekend. Mine is an aluminum 1/4" plate with a taper milled on the edge and 4 "L" brackets. The plate is the same size as the bottom of the scoop. It has a 6" X 3" oval cut out thru the decklid. I just place the scoop on and attach the front 2 bolts then press down the back and put in 2 more bolts. I have to do it this way because I get a good seal on the rubber gasket that is attached to the bottom edge of the scoop.<BR>There are metal washers epoxyed to the scoop where the bolts go so it doesn't damage the fiberglass of the scoop. I'm going to take pictures of the mount and placement of the scoop and post them. I'll try to get them up on Sunday but don't know yet.||||reg||1
